        "content": "\n| State | Load generator | TPS | Response time | What to do | Scenario to try |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ✅ **Healthy scalability** | More users | Rises in proportion | Flat, low | Keep going | 📈 TPS scales with users |\n| 🧮 **Not enough users** | Max users reached, requests skipped | Below target | Normal | Allow more users (≈ TPS × response time) | 🧮 Not enough users |\n| 🧱 **App bottleneck** | More users | Flattens | Climbs steeply; app queue > 0 | Optimise the app or add capacity | 🧱 App bottleneck |\n| 🥵 **Generator choke** | CPU ≈ 100%, event loop lagging | Drops / jumpy | Client ≫ server (false) | Use more or bigger generators | 🥵 Load generator overload |\n\n**Little's Law:** TPS = users ÷ (response time + think time), and in flight = TPS × response time. Run the scenarios from the load generator UI and watch the panels above react.\n"
